  "term": "hepatic encephalopathy",
  "definition": "Hepatic encephalopathy is a syndrome of brain and central nervous system dysfunction linked to liver failure, including problems related to portal-systemic shunting. It can involve reduced alertness and confusion that may worsen to coma, along with abnormal movement and reflex signs.",
